### bench::CpuFpWorkload::run_batch()
    one op = one double-precision FMA on one of 8 lanes; one iteration = 8 lane-FMAs
    GCC packed lanes 0-3 into a single ymm FMA and left lanes 4-7 scalar
function: 66 instructions; hot loop: 7 instructions
hot-loop mnemonics: vfmadd132sd x4, vfmadd132pd x1, sub x1, jne x1
expected: 1 packed x 4 doubles + 4 scalar = 8 lane-FMAs
  [OK  ] vfmadd132pd: expected 1, found 1
  [OK  ] vfmadd132sd: expected 4, found 4
  [OK  ] no separate vmul* in the loop (a split mul+add would mean the op is not a fused FMA): 0
--- hot loop ---
  90:	vfmadd132pd %ymm14,%ymm9,%ymm1
  95:	vfmadd132sd %xmm13,%xmm8,%xmm2
  9a:	sub    $0x1,%rax
  9e:	vfmadd132sd %xmm12,%xmm7,%xmm0
  a3:	vfmadd132sd %xmm11,%xmm6,%xmm4
  a8:	vfmadd132sd %xmm10,%xmm5,%xmm3
  ad:	jne    90 <bench::CpuFpWorkload::run_batch()+0x90>

